diff --git a/Documentation/hydrogen-performance-pack.txt b/Documentation/hydrogen-performance-pack.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0fc6971
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/hydrogen-performance-pack.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Hydrogen performance pack
+=========================
+
+This patch adds a conservative Android custom-kernel tuning pack:
+
+  - CONFIG_HYDROGEN_TWEAKS: boot-time VM/writeback tuning with runtime knobs at
+    /sys/kernel/hydrogen_tweaks/.
+  - hydrogen I/O scheduler: a tiny read-biased single-queue scheduler intended
+    for low UI latency on mobile UFS/eMMC queues that still use legacy elevators.
+  - zram default-compressor Kconfig choice; pissarro_defconfig selects lz4.
+  - pissarro_defconfig enables common compression, zram, F2FS compression,
+    EROFS compression, zswap/frontswap, KSM, BFQ, and the hydrogen scheduler.
+  - scripts/hydrogen/hydrogen-tune.sh: optional Android init.d/KernelSU/Magisk
+    helper for runtime scheduler, zram, VM and f2fs knobs.
+
+Boot parameters:
+
+  hydrogen_tweaks=0              Disable built-in Hydrogen VM tuning.
+  hydrogen_profile=balanced      balanced/performance/powersave.
+  hydrogen_profile=performance   Heavier dirty caching, lower VFS pressure.
+  hydrogen_profile=powersave     Smoother writeback, higher cache reclaim.
+
+Runtime examples:
+
+  cat /sys/kernel/hydrogen_tweaks/profile
+  echo performance > /sys/kernel/hydrogen_tweaks/profile
+  echo 90 > /sys/kernel/hydrogen_tweaks/vfs_cache_pressure
+  echo 0 > /sys/kernel/hydrogen_tweaks/page_cluster
+
+For I/O scheduler tuning after selecting hydrogen:
+
+  cat /sys/block/sda/queue/iosched/writes_starved
+  echo 2 > /sys/block/sda/queue/iosched/writes_starved
+  echo 1 > /sys/block/sda/queue/iosched/read_bias
+
+Notes:
+
+  - This patch intentionally does not raise charging thermal limits or disable
+    thermal protection.
+  - LZ4K/LZ4KD/UKSM-style feature ports are separate large code ports; this pack
+    enables the in-tree compression/memory features already available in this
+    kernel and adds small, reviewable mobile tuning code.
